- NEVER run `git commit` on your own. A commit happens only when I explicitly
  ask for one in this session ("commit", "کامیت بزن"). Finishing a task is NOT
  permission. When you reach a good commit point, say so and stop.
- Exception: skills whose contract includes a commit (`/fix-one`) — invoking
  them is the permission. One commit per invocation, nothing more.
- Never mention Claude, AI, or any assistant anywhere in a commit: no
  "Generated with Claude Code" footer, no `Co-Authored-By:` trailer, nothing
  in the message body or branch names. Write it as if I typed it myself.
- Branch naming: [e.g. feat/short-description]
- Commit messages: [e.g. Conventional Commits]
- Never commit without running `[typecheck]` and `[lint]` first.
- Never `git push --force` to a shared branch.

